  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`SqliteDomainDatabase(databaseFile)` declares the domain database by its file,** a `FileInfo`, with no configuration to give a connection string's name its connection string: SQLite's usual case, an application whose database is in a file it knows. SQLite creates the file at the database's first use, in a folder that must exist. In a testing container the file is used as it is, rather than a database of the test database pool.\n- **Disposing a container no longer leaves its SQLite database file open.** Microsoft.Data.Sqlite keeps the connections Compze closes open in a pool of its own, which held the file until the process ended, so on Windows the file couldn't be deleted or replaced. Disposing Compze's connection pool, as disposing the container does, now clears Microsoft.Data.Sqlite's pool for the database.",
